# The generated half of .agent/ must never be merged textually. Git would inject conflict markers
# into graph.json, making it invalid JSON — `godkit save` then refuses to overwrite it (correctly)
# and the map is stuck until someone hand-merges a machine-written node array.
#
# Resolve a conflict by taking either side — both are real graphs — then refreshing:
#   git checkout --ours .agent/graph.json .agent/meta.json .agent/MAP.md
#   godkit scan && ... && godkit save     # only the delta gets re-analyzed
#
# SKILLS.md is the same case, from `godkit evolve --write`: conflict markers there are cosmetic
# rather than fatal, but the only correct resolution is still to re-run the command that wrote it.
#
# The hand-written half (BOARD.md, THREAD.md, log/, tasks/, skills/) is deliberately NOT listed:
# those hold work a person or agent actually wrote, and a real textual merge is what you want.
# Note skills/ is the project's own SKILL.md sources — hand-written — while SKILLS.md above is
# the generated report about them. Different files, opposite treatment.
.agent/graph.json -merge
.agent/meta.json  -merge
.agent/MAP.md     -merge
.agent/SKILLS.md  -merge
